From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:02:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/18] fitz: Fix the sub-pixel position of vertically flipped
 scaled images.

fz_scale_pixmap_cached() took the sub-pixel offset of a vertically
flipped image from its bottom edge, while the weights count the rows
from the top, so an image at a fractional position was drawn as if
mirrored around the half pixel (at 30.25 as if at 30.75). The offset is
now taken from the top edge. Images on whole pixels, the usual case
after grid fitting, are unchanged.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/fitz/draw-scale-simple.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/fitz/draw-scale-simple.c b/source/fitz/draw-scale-simple.c
index 8a59695..7e7d1b8 100644
--- a/source/fitz/draw-scale-simple.c
+++ b/source/fitz/draw-scale-simple.c
@@ -1684,7 +1684,7 @@ fz_scale_pixmap_cached(fz_context *ctx, const fz_pixmap *src, float x, float y,
 		dst_y_int = floorf(y-h);
 		tmp = ceilf(y);
 		dst_h_int = (int)tmp;
-		y = tmp - y;
+		y = (y - h) - dst_y_int;
 		dst_h_int -= dst_y_int;
 	}
 	else
